.gradle/
build/
# A PATTERN with a leading slash, and the anchor is not decoration -- an unanchored `run*/` also
# swallows any `run/` directory nested under src/main/resources, which is where a datapack's
# structure folder could plausibly be called that. Rocketeer lost six templates to exactly this.
# A run directory is only ever created at the repo root, which is where gradle puts it.
/run*/
.claude/worktrees/
libs/
*.log
.idea/
*.iml
logs/
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__/
